00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
[Niko:] We are experimenting with some name changes and variations on the channel

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:09.200
So it's all part of that continuing process, trying to optimize and be the best channel we can possibly be

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.700
[Music by Johan Lilja]

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:32.320
So, we realize that our channel, just being "samandniko"-- all one word, all lowercase -- is not very good branding

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.740
[Carmichael:] Salmon Eagle.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.440
[Niko:] Salmon Eagle is the next alternative, but uh, we held off on that because it's

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.600
really cool and we want to wait for the right time to drop it.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.100
Also expect an icon change in the near future.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.140
Hey, you hear this, guys?

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:48.380
The first two videos that get 100,000 views -- in a row --  we get Carmichael(cmike) a new camera.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.760
[Carmichael:] Oh my god.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.160
Canon.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.060
For me?!

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.440
[Music by Johan Lilja]

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.580
Canon 80D!

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.420
[Grunt]

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:05.480
[Music by Johan Lilja]

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:08.940
Oh!

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.800
That looks fancy right there.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.120
Ho!

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.840
I opened it upside-down.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.960
[Sam:] Dude, these are the nicest camera bags.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.460
[Carmichael:] I know! [Sam:] Just bags?

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.800
[Carmichael:] We got lenses!

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.420
Full frame 1DX Mark 2.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.780
and then an 11 to 24.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.720
[Sam:] Alright, see, lookit, this is the new lens here.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.540
It's a-- it's a hair. It's a tiny little hair from a tiny little animal.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.600
let's test out this new lens, let's bring it for a ride.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.180
here we go guys, [Strained] new lens.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.820
[Grunts]

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.220
alright, how's that look?

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:42.820
[Off camera] - it's good.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.280
[Sam:] Whoa. That's such a big, bulbous lens.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.020
here's the old one.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.080
[Carmichael:] It's a full-- that's a full frame 11 mil. While that's a etsc 11 mil.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.820
[Sam:] That's gonna look crazy at 6K

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.000
[Niko:] Can I see your hat for a second?

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.040
[Sam:] Would you like to touch it?

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.300
[Niko:] I would like to touch your hat for a second. [laugh]

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.540
[laughs from everyone]

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.920
Corridor...Digital

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.840
Corridor...Digital

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.300
[Niko laughs]

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.600
The "Sam and Niko" channel isn't "Sam and Niko," it's Corridor.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.260
[Sam:] Then why don't we just go back to "C2?"

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:10.280
[Jake:] It's not a second channel

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.040
[Sam:] "Corridor Zero."

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.520
"Corridor 360."

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.360
[Niko:] Do you know why they called the "XBOX 360" the "XBOX 360?"

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.360
The real reason is because the XBOX original -- the "XBOX 1" -- came out when the PS2 came out.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.320
So when the next XBOX wanted to come out, they couldn't call it the XBOX 2,

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.460
cause the Playstation was at PS3.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.380
It would sound like it was a generation behind.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.300
So they also needed a "3" in their title. But they couldn't call it the XBOX 3

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.400
because they didn't have the second one.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.260
So they came up with the next most recognizable number that begins with 3

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.920
which is apparently "360."

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.100
So that's why it's totally arbitrary-

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:38.760
[Sam:] It's pretty good

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.460
[Niko:] Totally arbitrary

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.620
Favorite alternate channel name?

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.660
[mumbling]
[Off camera] - Yeah.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.980
[Sam:] What if you made that the word?

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.920
Rodirroc!

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.600
[everyone laughs]

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:48.840
[Niko:] Rodirroc!

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.480
[laughs continue]

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.280
[Charmichael:] [grunts] What lens is--

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.520
[Lens cover clattering on the ground]

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:00.500
This is not a gift, this is a loan from Canon. To experiment with some new lenses

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.520
new camerawork for the Sam and Niko channel and the Corridor channel

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.700
[Sam:] Exactly. You'll notice that obviously the lens says "MARKETING" on it

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.420
Sorry guys, we are actively marketing right now. Apologies for that

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.420
All those corporate lens industry product placement videos you see -- this is one of them

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.400
Macro 100

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.840
Let's do this. You wanna see something really really close up?

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.580
Alright, so this has gotta be pretty wonky lookin'

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.240
Boom.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.340
Yeah. Gross, right?

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.860
[Jake:] It's like a kid in Candy Land.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:30.700
[Sam:] Look at this.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:34.640
[Carmichael:] We got the 80D. 60 frames per second at 1080, which is great

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:40.320
And then the 1DX, 4K, 60 frames per second, and 120 frames, 1080

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.660
[Niko:] Are you excited, Carmichael?

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:42.800
I'm very excited

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.200
And...let's switch cameras.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.260
[Niko:] So here at Corridor, we make our living on YouTube.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.660
It's important for us to study the algorithms that suggests videos

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.000
and put your videos in front of new viewers.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.240
Kind of how the whole system works, because the more we understand that and learn that,

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.820
the better we can expand our audience

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.620
The Sam and Niko channel has gone through a pretty big evolution these last couple of months

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.180
[Wren:] How thick it was?

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.680
[Niko:] All the colors of the rainbow

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.360
[Sam:] Help

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.420
[Case being smashed]

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:09.540
[Wall being kicked]

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.220
[Sam:] You were shooting a little bit less, but it's all just a little bit better

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.040
[Steve:] Oh, I AM the camera!

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.280
Oh!

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:15.780
OH!

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.520
Oh -- OH SHIT!

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.520
[Niko:] A third of our audience watching Sam and Niko wasn't subscribed to the channel a month ago.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.880
We did a big subscription push.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.400
We had a couple segments of me speaking directly to the camera asking people to subscribe

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.940
and we did some little end cards that would politely say "Consider Subscribing"

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:31.860
And it worked great

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.560
Now we saw something interesting happen

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.120
I expected the percentage of unsubscribed viewers to dip

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:40.520
Previously it was 33%, now I expected it to go down to 30, maybe even 25%.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.380
But something interesting happened

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.160
Instead, the percentage of unsubscribed viewers on the channel-

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.460
[Air compressor running buzzing]

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:47.720
[laugh]

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.780
-but then the percentage actually went up

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:53.760
It went up from 33% unsubscribed, to 37% unsubscribed

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:54.980
And that's really strange

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:58.300
With thousands and thousands of new subscribers, we're getting more people

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.620
who are unsubscribed to the channel

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.220
So why is that, and how does the YouTube algorithm play into that?

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.140
I have a bit of a theory

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.160
[batman theme]

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.000
Now, this is pure speculation, YouTube's algorithm is secret

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.920
We don't know how it works, and we can only look at

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.760
the numbers on our computer screens to figure it out

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.280
So take this with a grain of salt

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:18.540
But, I think, that because the algorithm saw an uptick in engagement and subscribers

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.400
it flipped that little switch inside the system

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.580
that decided to put our content in front of even more viewers

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.180
in front of even more people

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:30.200
It would make sense that the algorithm would notice content bringing in viewers

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.860
and therefore put that content in front of even more viewers

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:37.220
And rank it up in search results, in suggested videos and all that kind of stuff

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:40.460
So in other words, by increasing our subscriber base

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:43.760
the algorithm then put our content in front of even more viewers

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.540
thereby increasing our percentage of unsubscribed viewers

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.020
Sounds backwards, but it worked

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.220
So when you guys are browsing Youtube and you're looking at different channels

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.300
Take a moment and  look at how they're doing at thumbnails, their titles, their strategies

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.520
everybody has all these different ideas as to what works the best

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.100
And if you have any ideas yourself, feel free to share them with us because we're all just trying to figure it out.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:05.840
[laughs]

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.700
[Music by Johan Lilja]

